/P 99 0 R
/E (only 20% of the labor force within Pakistan. Inequality in opportunities for work and limited ability for movement plays a strong role against their financial and economic empowerment. For those able to step into the workforce, additional barriers include a lack of gendered infrastructure at workplaces, limited mobility, gender pay gaps. scarcity of women-friendly public places, a dearth of public toilets, lack of job security, denial / discrimination of job opportunities among other factors.            )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [11]
>>
